      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:5:3:8",
      "text": [
        " قَالَ أَبُو الْحَسَنِ الرِّضَا ( عليه السلام ) إِذَا ذُبِحَتِ الشَّاةُ وَ سُلِخَتْ أَوْ سُلِخَ شَيْ‏ءٌ مِنْهَا قَبْلَ أَنْ تَمُوتَ لَمْ يَحِلَّ أَكْلُهَا ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, raising it, said, ",
          "‘Abu Al-Hassan Al-Reza<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘When you slaughter the sheep, and strip it, or strip off something from it before it dies, it is not Permissible to eat it’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "8. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from in a marfu‘ manner the following: “Abu al-Hassan, al-Rida’, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘When you slaughter a sheep and remove its skin or a certain part of its skin before it dies, it then is not lawful to use it for food.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
